<%#
  A notice that belongs to the page rather than to the request.

  The flash says "that worked"; a callout says "this is how things are here" -- the purchase is
  too old to edit, the kit cannot be recomposed once saved, this cannot be undone. It is
  rendered by the page, on every load, for as long as the condition holds.

    render "shared/essentials/callout", tone: :warning do
      ...the message, as ordinary markup...
    end

  Locals: tone (:info, :success, :warning, :danger), title, role, icon, wrapper_class.

  Sixteen copies of the same twelve-class string existed across fifteen files before this, each
  with its own margin baked in and no two agreeing on whether the role was status or alert. The
  tint, border and glyph come from FLASH_STYLES, the same map the flash strip uses, so the two
  cannot drift into different shades of amber.

  `wrapper_class` is for the margin only. A callout does not know where it sits, so spacing
  stays with the page that places it.
%>
<%
  # local_assigns, not defined?(): a partial compiled for a call site that passes `role:` keeps
  # `role` defined at the call sites that do not, so defined?(role) was true and nil there, and
  # every callout that relied on the default silently lost its role attribute.
  tone = local_assigns.fetch(:tone, :warning).to_sym
  style = essentials_flash_style(tone)
  title = local_assigns[:title]
  icon = local_assigns[:icon].presence || style[:icon]
  wrapper_class = local_assigns[:wrapper_class]
  callout_id = local_assigns[:callout_id]
  data = local_assigns.fetch(:data, {})
  # Same rule as the flash: interrupt only for the tones that mean something went wrong.
  # `role: nil` is honoured -- a callout that is plain page furniture is read in document order
  # and does not want a live region at all.
  role = local_assigns.key?(:role) ? local_assigns[:role] : ([:warning, :danger].include?(tone) ? "alert" : "status")
%>
<div class="flex items-start gap-2 rounded-2xl border px-4 py-3 text-sm <%= style[:bar] %> <%= wrapper_class %>"
     <%= tag.attributes(id: callout_id, role: role, **data) %>>
  <i class="<%= icon %> mt-0.5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
  <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
    <% if title %><p class="font-semibold"><%= title %></p><% end %>
    <%= yield %>
  </div>
</div>
